--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream inspiration and attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This application is an independent, local-first implementation inspired by the
interface and scope of:

    OmniGet
    https://github.com/OpenSelena/omniget
    Copyright (C) the OmniGet contributors
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0

The upstream project is a Tauri 2 + Rust + SvelteKit desktop application. This
build is not a fork of that source tree and contains no proprietary assets from
it. It reuses ideas, the general feature scope and the GPL-3.0 licensing model.
The mascot ("Pip"), logo, icon set, copy and application code in this build are
original work created for this implementation.

Because the upstream project is GPL-3.0 licensed and this work is distributed
under the same licence, the complete GPL-3.0 text is included in `LICENSE`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Runtime dependencies are declared in `package.json` and retain their own
licences. Notable components:

  - Svelte 5 and Vite (MIT)
  - Node.js built-in `node:sqlite` (MIT, Node.js)
  - pdf-lib (MIT) and PDF.js (Apache-2.0)
  - JSZip (MIT / GPL-3.0 dual)
  - Jimp (MIT)
  - cheerio (MIT)
  - marked (MIT)
  - qrcode (MIT) and jsQR (Apache-2.0)
  - busboy (MIT)
  - Inter, Bricolage Grotesque and IBM Plex Mono (SIL Open Font License 1.1),
    loaded from `@fontsource` packages.

Optional command-line tools are not bundled and are used only when already
installed on the host: ffmpeg/ffprobe (LGPL/GPL depending on build) and yt-dlp
(Unlicense). ZIP and PDF processing use the JavaScript dependencies listed
above, not external qpdf/zip binaries.

